WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Your next slide edit. Made together. An open-source companion for PowerPoint on macOS.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Start where you already work. This public test slide has three editable text boxes. No prompt or upload required.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Make the next step visible. The model proposes two arrows. Review first. Accept when ready.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.000
One accepted edit. Then the next. The next real suggestion adds numbered steps to the process.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Build on your decisions. A third suggestion groups the stages into outlined cards.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Keep going beyond three. A fourth accepted suggestion adds a heading to the slide.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Preview. Accept. Continue. Five consecutive accepted edits. Pause and resume were tested with the original file unsaved.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
No image upload required. The model chooses search terms from the solar-energy slide.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Search. Review. Insert. A Commons public-domain photo was inserted into PowerPoint. Source and credit stayed attached.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Your slides. Your final say. macOS preview / MIT github.com/genalyu/ppt-cursor Setup and limitations in README.
